Whether Fin of the list decoded from c1 is contained in Fin of the list decoded from c2 is recursively decidable.

The inclusion is equivalent to the statement that every index of the first decoded list has its basic neighbourhood in the second Fin family. The equivalence is the comparison of finitely generated families at the subsystem generated by the second list, and that pointwise statement is the bounded universal quantification of the decidable membership test for Fin.
